Z||000000||Orlando||08-17-99||10:34 AM||||at this very moment I'm having my 88 Formula serviced at the dealer. It's getting a new front (firewall side) exhaust manifold, a freon recharge (they say it's low, but there are no leaks?), and my 5spd transmission will be taken apart and resealed because it's leaking from the CV joint! I'm sure this leak will cause a big drain on my wallet. Anyway, here's me question - there's an 87 GT for sale where I live. It dosen't start, has a cruddy interior, and needs paint. The body is in good shape, and it has a sunroof. I can get it for $500. Should I buy it and swap the panels over to my 88, or should I swap engines (and interiors) and keep the 87?
Z||000001||Formula||08-17-99||03:05 PM||||I'd keep the formula because of the lotus suspension.
Z||000002||cmyokley||08-17-99||03:38 PM||||Ollando,<p>I too would keep the 88 with the upgradad suspension. The swap to put the GT back onto the 87 is not as bad as you would expect, just takes time. I have had my 86GT completely apart (every body panel), I would suggest one thing. The worst time I had on disassembly and assembly was the roof panel. I would suggest leaving the panel on your car unless you just want the sun roof. The roof panel was the worst for me.<p>Good Luck.
Z||000003||Orlando||08-17-99||05:52 PM||||Makes sense to me. If I keep the roof, should I have a body shop do the work? I can pretty basic repairs and I'm pretty good with a wrench. I just don't want a pile of parts sitting in the garage, and a car I can't drive for a month.<p>I'll make the deal this weekend.
Z||000004||Bill 88||08-18-99||08:02 AM||||Does the roof panel come off with-out to much trouble?  A auto body person told me that if I wanted to do that to my 88 with the top from the 86,  I would need to cut off the two tops and fiberglass/ bond the new top in.  Then look out for a weak top, possible leaks and/or wind whistle.
Z||000005||Orlando||08-18-99||06:25 PM||||Supposedly the some portion of te roof panel is glued on, but it can be pried off. After I buy this guys GT I may consider swapping the roof, but only after I get an estimate from a body shop on having them swap the panels.
Z||000006||cmyokley||08-19-99||12:03 PM||||Guys, the swap is not too hard, there are several bolts under the heqad liner to take out, some bolts on each side under the slotted vents by the rear engine cover and if I remember several bolts that you can see after removing the tail lights. My 16 year old son and I removed (and installed) all the panels on the car without too many problems. Like I said on 17AUG the top was the worst. Do not let anyone tell you you need to cut the tops and glue them back together???A sunroof top is just like one with out the sunfoof in the way it was designed and can be swapped if you have time. You will need to be very careful with the two thin pieces thet go along the windshield. They are glued on with black rubbery stuff so take it slow so as not to break them off. Take pictures when disassembling the car...they will come in very handy when you put the panels back on.
